pysisyphus 1.0.0: 0009-irc-energy-increase-stop-optional

What: IRC(stop_on_energy_increase=False) no longer ends a direction when one step raises the energy; each rise is recorded in self.energy_rises. pysisyphus 1.0.0 always stops there and has no setting to turn it off.
Test: Tertiary hydride shift (M06-2X), forward side, before the fix: stopped after 7 points, 0.015 kJ/mol below the TS, on a noise-level rise (per-step changes 0.001-0.003 kJ/mol, below the SCF scatter of 0.034 kJ/mol); rerun with the stop off (2026-11-14). Diels-Alder forward stopped at its minimum on a 1.6e-6 kJ/mol rise.

